        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.752,
            0.046,
            0.862,
            0.064
          ],
          "content": "Number Play"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.087,
            0.848,
            0.128
          ],
          "content": "Eight such expressions are possible. You can use the diagram below to systematically list all the possibilities."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.23,
            0.135,
            0.711,
            0.355
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_1_image_3.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.109,
            0.366,
            0.85,
            0.408
          ],
          "content": "Evaluate each expression and write the result next to it. Do you notice anything interesting?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.413,
            0.808,
            0.473
          ],
          "content": "? Now, take four other consecutive numbers. Place the ‘+’ and ‘–’ signs as you have done before. Find out the results of each expression. What do you observe?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.479,
            0.808,
            0.52
          ],
          "content": "? Repeat this for one more set of 4 consecutive numbers. Share your findings."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.823,
            0.459,
            0.911,
            0.511
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_1_image_7.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.835,
            0.474,
            0.884,
            0.507
          ],
          "content": "Math Talk"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.181,
            0.532,
            0.335,
            0.552
          ],
          "content": "3+4-5+6=8",
          "image_source": "images/page_1_equation_9.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.396,
            0.532,
            0.565,
            0.553
          ],
          "content": "5+6-7+8=12",
          "image_source": "images/page_1_equation_10.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.182,
            0.552,
            0.359,
            0.572
          ],
          "content": "3 - 4 - 5 - 6 = -12",
          "image_source": "images/page_1_equation_11.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.396,
            0.552,
            0.575,
            0.572
          ],
          "content": "5-6-7-8=16",
          "image_source": "images/page_1_equation_12.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.669,
            0.807,
            0.709
          ],
          "content": "Some sums appear always no matter which 4 consecutive numbers are chosen. Isn’t that interesting?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.71,
            0.807,
            0.751
          ],
          "content": "？ Do these patterns occur no matter which 4 consecutive numbers are chosen? Is there a way to find out through reasoning?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.752,
            0.806,
            0.774
          ],
          "content": "**Hint:** Use algebra and describe the 8 expressions in a general form."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.779,
            0.848,
            0.854
          ],
          "content": "You might have noticed that the results of all expressions are even numbers. Even numbers have a factor of 2. Negative numbers having a factor 2 are also even numbers, for example, $- 2 , - 4 , - 6 ,$ and so on. Check if anyone in your class got an odd number."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.853,
            0.848,
            0.911
          ],
          "content": "When 4 consecutive numbers are chosen, no matter how the ‘+’ and ‘–’ signs are placed between them, the resulting expressions always have even parity."
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.873,
